{"step_index":159,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-11T23:35:41Z","thinking":"**Deriving radius upper bound**\n\nAnalyzing the provided relations, the goal is to deduce an upper bound for the radius. Starting with the inequalities involving domination numbers and radius, consider how to link them.\nFirst, combine `total_domination_number <= 2 domination_number` and `roman_domination_number <= 2 total_domination_number` to get a relation between `roman_domination_number` and `domination_number`, while keeping the radius in mind.\n\nConsider Challenge_e20263a9 and Challenge_40a99333. The goal is to combine the inequalities.\nFrom `radius <= total_domination_number`, and `total_domination_number <= roman_domination_number`, it can be inferred that radius <= roman_domination_number. Challenge_e20263a9 tells `(nontrivial) ⇒ (radius + 1) ≤ roman_domination_number`, which means that it can be simplified as `radius + 1 <= roman_domination_number`, or `radius <= roman_domination_number - 1`.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"run_command","args":{"CommandLine":"\"/mnt/home/japake298/project/GraphConjecturing/.venv/bin/python -c \\\"\\nimport networkx as nx\\nfrom itertools import combinations\\n\\ndef total_domination_number(G):\\n    n = G.number_of_nodes()\\n    nodes = list(G.nodes())\\n    # check each subset size k from 1 to n\\n    for k in range(1, n + 1):\\n        for S in combinations(nodes, k):\\n            S_set = set(S)\\n            # check if every node has a neighbor in S\\n            if all(any(nbr in S_set for nbr in G.neighbors(v)) for v in nodes):\\n                return k\\n    return None\\n\\nfound_counter = False\\nfor n in range(2, 10):\\n    for G in nx.graph_atlas_g():\\n        if G.number_of_nodes() == n and nx.is_connected(G):\\n            rad = nx.radius(G)\\n            td = total_domination_number(G)\\n            if rad > td:\\n                print(f'Counterexample found! n={n}, rad={rad}, td={td}, edges={list(G.edges())}')\\n                found_counter = True\\n                break\\n    if found_counter:\\n        break\\nif not found_counter:\\n    print('Checked all connected graphs in graph atlas (up to n=7)! No counterexample!')\\n\\\"\"","Cwd":"\"/mnt/home/japake298/project/GraphConjecturing/handoff/promising13/task_2a2555cc\"","WaitMsBeforeAsync":"10000","toolAction":"\"Running command\"","toolSummary":"\"Check graph atlas for counterexamples\""}}]}
